{"id":"652341a3ff50e1e3159da5f95524d59806396decad49afae90d8f073aef5cb76","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-09-27T11:01:42.483955907Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-09-27T11:01:42.483955907Z","created-by":"scual.project@gmail.com","description":"`ti list --depends-on X` and `ti list --blocks X` return direct relations only (decided in 2870b8). Users sometimes need the full chain: everything upstream of X (all transitive blockers) or everything downstream (all transitive dependents), with the chain structure visible.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Where it lives: `ti show` section, a new `ti deps`/graph command, or a `--recursive` list flag (a flat list hides the chain, so a tree is preferred).\n- How closed intermediates are treated: if A depends on B (closed) and B depends on C (open), does C still block A? `ti next` only checks direct dependencies.\n- Output formats: tree for humans, JSON/Markdown for agents.\n\nRelated: 2870b8.","state":"new","status":"open","title":"Transitive / tree view of ticket Dependencies"}}}